{#
settings/_sorting.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What sorts this person's mail into tabs, and whether it outranks the provider.

Two independent questions, two forms, exactly like the compose-behaviour card
beside it: each control submits on change, and a shared form would post both
keys whenever either moved. The controller writes only the key it is sent, so
they cannot overwrite one another.

The same two-segment idiom every boolean on these pages wears.

Accepts:
  source            'rules' | 'assistant'
  overrideProvider  bool
  assistantOffered  bool — whether categorisation is available to this person
                    at all. The choice is still SHOWN when it is not, because
                    hiding a setting is how somebody concludes the feature does
                    not exist; it is disabled and says why instead.
#}
{% set segText = 'flex h-full items-center justify-center px-3 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                  peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                  peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                  peer-disabled:opacity-50 peer-disabled:cursor-not-allowed
                  transition-colors cursor-pointer' %}

<div class="px-4 py-3">

<form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_sorting_update') }}" data-turbo="false" data-controller="ui--auto-submit">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-sorting') }}">

    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.sorting.source.label'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">
                {{ ('settings.sorting.source.' ~ source ~ '_help')|trans }}
            </span>
        </span>

        <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
             role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ 'settings.sorting.source.label'|trans }}">
            {% for option in ['rules', 'assistant'] %}
                <label>
                    {# The assistant option is refused rather than hidden when
                       categorisation is not available: an administrator has to
                       switch it on for the installation and the reader has to
                       not have switched it off for themselves, and a control
                       that vanished would leave somebody wondering which. #}
                    <input type="radio" name="source" class="peer sr-only"
                           value="{{ option }}"
                           data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                           {{ 'assistant' == option and not assistantOffered ? 'disabled' : '' }}
                           {{ source == option ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="{{ segText }}">
                        {{ ('settings.sorting.source.' ~ option)|trans }}
                    </span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {% if not assistantOffered %}
        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-2">{{ 'settings.sorting.source.unavailable'|trans }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</form>

<form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_sorting_update') }}" data-turbo="false" class="mt-4" data-controller="ui--auto-submit">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-sorting') }}">

    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.sorting.override.label'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.sorting.override.hint'|trans }}</span>
        </span>

        <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
             role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ 'settings.sorting.override.label'|trans }}">
            {% for override in [false, true] %}
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="overrideProvider" class="peer sr-only"
                           value="{{ override ? '1' : '0' }}"
                           data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                           {{ overrideProvider == override ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="{{ segText }}">
                        {{ (override ? 'settings.sorting.override.plmail' : 'settings.sorting.override.provider')|trans }}
                    </span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

{# Asking again, which is a different thing from either control above.

   Those decide what sorts the mail; this re-asks the model about mail it has
   already answered for. It exists because the ANSWER goes stale while the mail
   does not: the prompt is editable, the model is a setting, and what plMail
   sends alongside a message has changed. Nothing re-asks on its own, because a
   model call per message is the most expensive thing here.

   Only where the assistant can actually be used. On a rules-only installation
   there is no verdict to refresh and the button would be an offer that does
   nothing. #}
{% if assistantOffered %}
    <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_sorting_again') }}" data-turbo="false" class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-line">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-sorting') }}">

        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
            <span class="min-w-0">
                <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.sorting.again.label'|trans }}</span>
                <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.sorting.again.hint'|trans }}</span>
            </span>

            <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0">
                {# A count and not a free number: the cost is model calls on a
                   host everybody shares, and three sizes is the whole of the
                   decision anybody actually has. #}
                <select name="limit"
                        class="h-8 rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface px-2 text-[11px] text-ink-muted cursor-pointer">
                    {% for size in [100, 200, 500] %}
                        <option value="{{ size }}" {{ 200 == size ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ size }}</option>
                    {% endfor %}
                </select>

                <button type="submit"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 h-8 px-3 rounded-pane border border-line
                               text-[11px] text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover cursor-pointer transition-colors">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'settings.sorting.again.button'|trans }}
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
{% endif %}

{# Said once, under both, because it is true of both and it is the question
   anybody will have: what happens to the mail already in the tabs. It is
   re-filed, in the background, and a large mailbox takes a few minutes — which
   is worth saying, because a tab that has not changed yet otherwise reads as a
   setting that did nothing. #}
<p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-line">
    {{ 'settings.sorting.applies_to_new'|trans }}
</p>

</div>
